        "original_id": "2072ce39-9bdd-5074-a926-88342f1b5ca6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mervyn Peake, Robert Erskine Childers, Gretchen Osgood Warren, Mary Alden Childers, Hamilton Osgood, Margaret Cushing Osgood\n- Works: Gormenghast books, The Riddle of the Sands, Titus Alone, Asgard\n- Places: Beacon Hill, Boston, Massachusetts, Ireland\n- Topics: British writers, Irish nationalism, Fenian revolutionaries\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Erskine Childers was born on 25 June 1870 and died on 24 November 1922.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was universally known as Erskine Childers.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was a British writer whose works included the influential novel The Riddle of the Sands.\n- Robert Erskine Childers was also a Fenian revolutionary who smuggled guns to Ireland in his sailing yacht Asgard.\n- Titus Alone is a novel by Mervyn Peake that was first published in 1959.\n- Mervyn Peake is best known for the books usually referred to as the Gormenghast books.\n- Gretchen Osgood Warren was the daughter of Dr. Hamilton Osgood and Margaret Cushing Osgood of Beacon Hill, Boston, Massachusetts.\n- Mary Alden Childers was the younger sister of Gretchen Osgood Warren and the wife of writer and Irish nationalist Robert Erskine Childers.",
